*   $\partial_{[\mu}$: This represents the antisymmetrized partial derivative operator with respect to the spacetime index $\mu$. The square brackets around the indices $[\mu 
u \lambda]$ denote antisymmetrization over these indices. Explicitly, $\partial_{[\mu} F_{
u\lambda]} =  rac{1}{3!} (\partial_\mu F_{
u\lambda} + \partial_
u F_{\lambda\mu} + \partial_\lambda F_{\mu
u} - \partial_\mu F_{\lambda
u} - \partial_
u F_{\mu\lambda} - \partial_\lambda F_{
u\mu})$. Due to the antisymmetry of $F_{\mu
u}$ itself ($F_{\mu
u} = -F_{
u\mu}$), this simplifies to $ rac{1}{3} (\partial_\mu F_{
u\lambda} + \partial_
