u})$. It is a differential operator with units of inverse length ($	ext{m}^{-1}$). 
*   $F_{
u\lambda}$: This is the electromagnetic field strength tensor, a rank-2 antisymmetric tensor that combines the electric field $\mathbf{E}$ and magnetic field $\mathbf{B}$ into a single relativistic entity. Its components are measured in units of Volts per meter ($	ext{V/m}$) or Newtons per Coulomb ($	ext{N/C}$) in SI units.
*   $\mu, 
u, \lambda$: These are spacetime indices, ranging from $0, 1, 2, 3$ (representing time and three spatial dimensions) in Minkowski spacetime. They are dimensionless labels.
*   $\equiv 0$: This signifies that the expression is identically zero, meaning it holds true for all spacetime points and all valid electromagnetic fields, reflecting a fundamental consistency condition.
